--TEST--
`Core\Command::run` throws for a `#[Command]` parameter no argument's text is converted into yet, rather than guessing — ADR 0086 § 6
--FILE--
<?nvs
// § 6 admits an enum among the types an argument may be given at, and this
// runtime does not convert one yet: `nvs_runtime::commands`'s gap 1 is an enum
// and a union of literal types, both of which need the *closed set* the
// compiler holds carried on the row beside the conversion. The two wrong
// answers are a plausible first case and a usage error blaming the command
// line, so it is neither: a `LogicError`, which is what a mistake in the
// *program* is, since the table is fixed at compile time and no input can
// change what this row declares.
enum Level {
    Quiet,
    Loud,
}

class Radio {
    #[Core\Command(name: "tune")]
    public static function tune(Level $level): uint {
        echo "tune ran\n";
        return 0;
    }
}

try {
    uint $status = Core\Command::run();
    echo "status: ", $status, "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
--ARGS--
tune
Loud
--EXPECT--
`Core\Command::run` cannot convert an argument into the type `tune`'s `level` is declared at yet
